{"id": "EUVD-2026-82130", "enisaUuid": "6315b422-9318-33dd-9da8-f8306ffdf1c0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/core: Fix potential use after free in counter_release()\n\nWhen accessing a counter via the netlink path the only synchronization\nmechanism for the said counter is rdma_restrack_get().\nCurrently, rdma_restrack_del() is invoked at the end of\ncounter_release(), which is too late, since by that point\nvendor-specific resources associated with the counter might already be\nfreed. This can leave a short window where the counter remains\naccessible through restrack, leading to a potential use-after-free.\n\nFix this by moving the rdma_restrack_del() call to be before the\nfreeing of the vendor-specific resources, ensuring that the counter is\nremoved from restrack before its internal resources are released.\nThis guarantees that no new users hold references to a counter that is\nin the process of destruction.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:04:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5eb0c57a8b568eb08f464861d84d518a2af939ac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d5cc211e8c39e46f357d30a092d683e84d560de9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f0c6705e26ba92c0c6b0b0908a2d3f35a039d5b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8c013e3a8d8273da4d47bf1c27f016a3551996f5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64c72390d8407ea86de712a477c796b07d37abc4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/235ef2d0e750885c29340b0fc40620a7a4f52e12"], "aliases": ["GHSA-w9c6-3cwc-m3q4", "CVE-2026-92509"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "001f15ba-1345-3469-ba74-6b4afd1dcec1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "12c88f23-a894-33c1-b016-3e20e506fbe0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "6d748e35-09ed-364c-9fe8-912500316f76", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.3"}, {"id": "7e0e03fa-5290-348f-ad20-d2c3cd4bd9d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "8149c05c-4279-3f4d-b77c-0766a6fac918", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "99fa331dc8629be55ac7a0cca0dc56492070ddac <2f0c6705e26ba92c0c6b0b0908a2d3f35a039d5b"}, {"id": "860992b4-2f8c-3683-9f12-c092930d3f13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "af79e6ad-d302-36e8-a811-9fc4d726bcdd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b065a01c-6db7-361f-b8d0-9f4643d56d15", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "b31e0c80-8065-38aa-9f28-6a3131b3ccc4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "99fa331dc8629be55ac7a0cca0dc56492070ddac <5eb0c57a8b568eb08f464861d84d518a2af939ac"}, {"id": "b932c2bb-4c93-3ac3-92d6-28d780921c52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "99fa331dc8629be55ac7a0cca0dc56492070ddac <8c013e3a8d8273da4d47bf1c27f016a3551996f5"}, {"id": "c9ee4a00-b389-3cfe-a3ec-f699e1b03814", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "99fa331dc8629be55ac7a0cca0dc56492070ddac <d5cc211e8c39e46f357d30a092d683e84d560de9"}, {"id": "ddde5054-5252-3e56-9d5c-69d674bea8f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "99fa331dc8629be55ac7a0cca0dc56492070ddac <235ef2d0e750885c29340b0fc40620a7a4f52e12"}, {"id": "ee078b78-817a-32e8-acb1-93d994cae824", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "99fa331dc8629be55ac7a0cca0dc56492070ddac <64c72390d8407ea86de712a477c796b07d37abc4"}, {"id": "f3dd72bd-ecb5-3b25-a781-e313ecee4bbc", "product": {"name": "Linux",